# Candelabra of Tawnos is "{X}, {T}: Untap X target lands". X is announced first (CR 601.2b), then the targets
# (CR 601.2c), and only then are mana abilities activated and the cost paid (CR 601.2g-h, via 602.2b). So the two
# untapped Islands can be the targets and then be tapped to pay the {X} of 2 — and they untap as the ability resolves.

[Bot1 Deck]
Candelabra of Tawnos
Island
Island
Island x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x16

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Candelabra of Tawnos.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Candelabra of Tawnos.Activate(X: 2)
Bot1.Target(Bot1.Battlefield.Island; Bot1.Battlefield.Island#2)
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Island#2.Activate

[Expect]
Turn = 3
Bot1.Battlefield.Candelabra of Tawnos.Tapped = true
Bot1.Battlefield.Island#1.Tapped = false
Bot1.Battlefield.Island#2.Tapped = false
